    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-12T22:09:49+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-12T22:09:49+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-12T12:39:49Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-12T12:39:49Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A trough is approaching from the west and will move across SA on Sunday, as an upper level disturbance moves over the far west later on Sunday. A high pressure ridge will also extend into the state from a high located southwest of WA from late Sunday. A cold front will then slip across southern coasts late Monday and early Tuesday, before the high moves across waters to the south to be centred over Victoria by Thursday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-12T22:07:37+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-13T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-12T12:37:37Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-12T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the far west, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Winds northerly 15 to 20 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-13T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-14T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-12T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-13T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower south of Coober Pedy in the early morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h in the morning then tending southeast to southwesterly in the late afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 18 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 33.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 3:40pm, UV Index predicted to reach 8 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-14T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-15T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-13T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-14T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog south of Coober Pedy. Medium chance of showers in the far west, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Winds southeast to southwesterly 15 to 20 km/h becoming light before dawn then becoming southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 16 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 29.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-15T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-16T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-14T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-15T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower in the far west, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm in the far west in the morning. Winds south to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending east to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 9 and 15 with daytime temperatures reaching 21 to 26.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-09-16T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-17T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-15T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-16T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Sunny. Winds east to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
